  "summary": "Paducah, Kentucky has 32 Flock Safety cameras deployed, and Police Chief Brian Laird defends the program citing quarterly audits, documented access, and arrests made using the system. A local resident raises privacy concerns about cameras in residential areas, and the article notes the broader national trend of cities ending Flock contracts, including Denver's removal of 110 cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "we have strict policies related to accessing that data; for our officers to have access to that data, there has to be a reason, and that's documented. We conduct audits quarterly on access into the Flock system",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We do share our information or access into our camera systems with hundreds of police departments all across the country",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "putting a Flock camera in a residential area facing individuals' properties, that is a concern to me, because that's constant monitoring",
